      "message": "feat(threadmill)!: thread-mill tool kinds and a reworked helical thread-milling operation\n\nTool model: two new kinds, thread_mill (multi-form: rows of teeth at one\npitch) and thread_mill_single (single-form: one row, a pitch range), with\nthe new Tool field pitch_min. Sanity law, pitch door and form door in\ncamcraft-tools::thread_mill; library and project file round-trip; the tool\neditor, the tree, the operation digest; two starter-catalog tools. The\nprogram simulation sweeps a thread mill at its tooth roots, as it does a tap.\n\nThread operation: the kernel is rewritten. Radial passes are full helices\n(equal steps, the last on the ISO thread depth); a single-form mill winds one\nturn per thread, a multi-form mill one revolution per level; tangential lead\narcs that keep the helix's axial rate; climb / conventional and right / left\nhand by the handbook rule under an M3 spindle; the tip never below the floor,\nno rapid below the feature's top; the feed stated at the cutting edge and\nprogrammed at the tool centre. The operation gains pitch (optional) and hand.\nThe old ride could not post at all (the crossing and tangency laws convicted\nevery move), cut the top threads shallower than the bottom ones, and wound a\nleft-hand helix under its default setting.\n\nGouge laws: the tooth crests are judged against the thread's major circle\n(tangency), the body under the teeth against the part solid with no allowance\nat the tip (solid law); the crossing law stands down for Thread only.\n\nRefusals by name when the operation is made, edited, retyped or re-tooled and\nagain at generate: a pitch outside the tool's range or other than a\nmulti-form mill's, a form other than 60 degrees, an infeed past the thread\ndepth, a mill no smaller than a hole's minor diameter.\n\nExternal threads are cut by the kernel (pinned, golden) but not yet offered\nby the operation (#985). Still owed: the thread form in the simulation\n(#986), other thread forms (#987), pass controls (#988), the MCP skill text\n(#989). Decisions and sources: docs/decisions/894-thread-mill.md.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a Thread operation no longer accepts a Tap-kind tool; an\nexisting one names its tool and refuses to generate until the tool is\nre-kinded as a thread mill. Every existing Thread operation reads Stale once\nand regenerates to the new ride. Tool gains the field pitch_min.\n\nRefs #894\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
